      <h1>Korean &amp; Japanese Battery Manufacturers</h1>
      <p class="muted">Manufacturer Directory · Last reviewed 2026-09</p>

      <div class="box">
        <strong>Direct answer:</strong> Korea contributes the <strong>lithium trio</strong> —
        <strong>LG Energy Solution, SK On, Samsung SDI</strong> — global EV cell leaders. Japan contributes
        <strong>Panasonic Energy</strong> (EV cells), <strong>GS Yuasa</strong> (lead-acid + industrial lithium)
        and <strong>AESC</strong> (EV cells, now China-Japan-based). Together they are the non-Chinese half of
        East Asia's battery industry.
      </div>

